WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.799 --> 00:00:18.011
Instead of exporting files, you can connect accounts directly. Every connector accepts your own API keys or tokens.

2
00:00:18.011 --> 00:00:26.412
Keys are encrypted at rest with AES-256 and never sent back to the browser. Use app passwords and short-lived tokens where you can.

3
00:00:26.412 --> 00:00:34.175
IMAP works with Gmail, Outlook, Fastmail, iCloud and any mail server. It scans your inbox and sent folder for two-way conversations.

4
00:00:34.175 --> 00:00:40.215
Google uses the Gmail and People APIs. Microsoft 365 uses Microsoft Graph for mail and contacts.

5
00:00:40.215 --> 00:00:55.961
X resolves followers and follows with names and avatars from a bearer token. Facebook and LinkedIn verify your account with their tokens.

6
00:00:55.961 --> 00:01:01.221
Fill in the host, your address and an app password, then connect.

7
00:01:01.221 --> 00:01:07.571
The connector appears with its settings; notice the password is only shown as set, never its value.

8
00:01:07.571 --> 00:01:15.792
Test checks the credentials. Sync now pulls everything in and runs the same matching as a file import.

9
00:01:15.792 --> 00:01:25.107
Connected accounts also show on the Import page, so you can sync from the same place you import files.

10
00:01:25.107 --> 00:01:29.270
Remove a connector at any time; its keys are deleted with it.
